I see the issue! Looking at your CSS, I found the problem. The white space is actually coming from the cards themselves, not the main content padding. Notice that all your cards have margin-bottom: 25px and the col-md-* classes have padding-left: 15px and padding-right: 15px.

But more importantly, I see you have conflicting sidebar styles. You have the sidebar defined as position: fixed in one place and position: relative in another. Here's the fix:

Find and REMOVE this entire block (around line 40-50):

```css
/* Sidebar Styles */
.sidebar {
    min-height: 100vh;
    width: var(--sidebar-width);
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
    color: white;
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 1000;
    transition: var(--transition);
    box-shadow: 3px 0 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}
```

Then, MODIFY this block (around line 85-95) to add left: 0:

Find this:

```css
/* Sidebar fix for flex layout */
.sidebar {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: var(--sidebar-width);
    position: relative;
    min-height: 100vh;
}
```

Change it to:

```css
/* Sidebar fix for flex layout */
.sidebar {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: var(--sidebar-width);
    position: relative;
    min-height: 100vh;
    left: 0;  /* ADD THIS LINE */
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--primary), var(--secondary)); /* ADD THIS LINE */
    color: white; /* ADD THIS LINE */
    box-shadow: 3px 0 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); /* ADD THIS LINE */
}
```

Then, to remove the white space BETWEEN sidebar and content, add this CSS:

Add this anywhere in your CSS (I suggest near the top of your main-content section):

```css
/* Remove gap between sidebar and content */
.d-flex {
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: flex-start;
    width: 100%;
    gap: 0; /* ADD THIS - removes any gap between flex items */
}

/* Ensure no margin or padding creates space */
.sidebar {
    margin-right: 0;
    padding-right: 0;
}

.main-content {
    margin-left: 0;
    padding-left: 0;
}

/* But keep internal card spacing */
.main-content .card:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
}

/* Adjust column padding inside main-content */
.main-content [class*="col-"] {
    padding-left: 15px;
    padding-right: 15px;
}

/* First column in a row shouldn't have left padding */
.main-content .row [class*="col-"]:first-child {
    padding-left: 15px; /* Keep this for visual balance inside content */
}

/* Remove any default body margin that might affect layout */
body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}
```

If you still see white space, it might be coming from the .container-fluid or body background

Add this to ensure no background bleed-through:

```css
/* Ensure no background creates visible gap */
.container-fluid {
    background-color: #f8f9fa; /* Match your body background */
}

.sidebar {
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
}
```

The main issue was that you had two conflicting sidebar definitions - one with position: fixed and one with position: relative. The fixed positioning was likely pulling the sidebar out of the normal flow and creating weird spacing. By removing the fixed positioning and using only the flex layout version, the sidebar will sit flush against the main content.
